{"id": "EUVD-2026-108649", "enisaUuid": "c91c6128-c6a2-321b-8df3-e83f36007435", "description": "gose parsed the JWS `crit` header into `JwsHeader.Crit` and then never read it. RFC 7515 \u00a74.1.11 requires a recipient to reject a JWS whose listed critical extension parameters it does not understand. gose implements no header extensions, so every token carrying a non-empty `crit` should have been rejected \u2014 and none were.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T08:50:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T08:50:22", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/eclipse-keypont/gose/security/advisories/GHSA-445r-fpvv-hgwc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89317"], "assigner": "eclipse", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1a01447c-b561-3bb2-a724-3c0b125fc1b9", "product": {"name": "Eclipse KeyPont - GOSE", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}, "product_version": "0.7.3 \u22640.13.0-rc1"}, {"id": "eba59041-bc2c-3056-9b4e-7e0e6da63cca", "product": {"name": "Eclipse KeyPont - GOSE", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.0.0-rc4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7f5fb106-33fb-3a76-a3ec-df1c522f2da4", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}], "isExploited": false}